    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0107" n="39" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg39"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2078</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: You have undoubtedly
                    read the flimsy of Mr. Page’s 2716, August 29, two p. m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d40-f1"/> relative to the attack on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Nicosian</hi> and the events which followed. To me the conduct of the
                    British naval authorities is shocking, and I sincerely hope that this matter may
                    not become public, as it would seriously affect public opinion in Germany and
                    might result in retaliatory measures of a most rigorous character.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
